TIP:  There’s only to chords but the movement from the (G) to the (D) drags, and can be a little tricky.  You need to hold onto the (G) until the last moment and then change to the (D) at the tail end of the syllable.

TIP:  The (D) at the end of the verse (e.g., “cinnamon”) gets a full strum measure, otherwise you’ll move to the next (G) in the interlude too quickly.

TIP:  The strumming pattern is very important to the song and it’s down, down-up, up-down-up.  If you ever find yourself lost just come back to it with the first downstrum at the chord change.
  

